{"description":"Test coverage was inversely related to blast radius. `metadata` — through which every eka.yaml read passes — sat at 47.3%, the lowest in the module, with `EffectiveCapture`, `parseDedupeWindow` and most of `Marshal` at zero. In `runtime`, the capture dedupe logic that decides whether a task is recorded or merged into an existing draft was entirely uncovered. A single module-wide coverage number hid all of it, because the large, well-covered packages dominated the total.","impact":"The untested code was not incidental: `EffectiveCapture` governs whether capture runs at all and over what window, and `Marshal` produces the byte format other tooling diffs. Coverage is now measured and enforced per package (`scripts/coverage.floor`, `scripts/coverage-gate.sh` wired into CI) so a drop in one package fails the build instead of being averaged away by the other twelve. metadata is 95.6%, runtime 65.3%."}